{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## HANDOFF-2E47: two criteria left, both waiting on ONE dispatched harness run\n\nGerrit 1375, 1381, 1389, 1390 all merged. Remaining unchecked:\n\n    - [ ] the duplicate `Task` name is handled by resolving types by ID, or the ambiguity is\n          documented as harmless with evidence\n    - [ ] the declared environment contract (3fe5) asserts these so a future instance change fails loudly\n\n**Both are answered by harness run 30951453979** (dispatched, `main` @ `d394a7052`, ~45 min).\n\nWhat to look for in that run's `jira DC harness smoke` job log:\n\n    [2e47-issue-type-evidence] project RBJxxxx offers [...]; instance-wide entries matching\n      ['Task','Sub-task','Epic'] (GET /rest/api/2/issuetype -> HTTP 200): [...]\n\n* **If the run reaches the tests at all, the assertion already passed** — `_assert_project_capabilities`\n  raises at provisioning when a project offers an issue-type NAME more than once. So a run that executes\n  tests IS the evidence that the duplicate `Task` ids do NOT reach the project scheme a create binds\n  against. That is the \"documented as harmless with evidence\" branch; resolving types by ID is then\n  unnecessary.\n* The evidence LINE is the positive record. It did not print in run 30944241768 because of a bug of mine\n  (the list was built from `/rest/api/2/field` filtered against issue-type names, so it could never\n  match, and a conditional guard hid it) — fixed in 1390, now unconditional with the HTTP status.\n* Also re-run in that job: the label-ceiling cell with its CORRECTED assertion (255 accepted, 256\n  probed). It should now PASS. If 255 is suddenly rejected, the divergence is real after all and\n  [rebar:2c93-ce1c-127e-4d58] must be re-opened — the assertion message says so.\n\nThen: tick both, and close (`--class env_integration` fits — the findings were instance-vocabulary\nmismatches, one of which did not reproduce).\n\nStill deliberately OUT of scope and tracked elsewhere: the per-deployment label ceiling\n[rebar:2c93-ce1c-127e-4d58], now largely moot since the divergence did not reproduce — its first\ncriterion (measure Cloud's 255) is the honest way to close it."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785878505995987001,"uuid":"144db7a1-484f-4b00-9fa7-7694162e2191"}